    "Scouting Notes": "Really good bat to ball skills\n Makes great swing decisions\n Has pretty decent pop in the bat, but the swing is most likely not going to put up huge home run numbers. Line drive approach.\n Not a good infield defender, would not feel very good about him anywhre on the infield\n Definitely an outfielder in my opinion\n Good speed, capable base stealer, though likely not the big time one we saw in 2023 at AA\n Still like the guy offensively, but feels like someone they might trade",
    "Notes Updated 2": "6/20/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Really good bat to ball skills\n  Makes great swing decisions\n  Has pretty decent pop in the bat, but the swing is most likely not going to put up huge home run numbers. Line drive approach.\n  Not a good infield defender, would not feel very good about him at second base.\n  Surprisingly has looked solid in center field. Likely moves to left as he goes higher up the ranks.\n  Good speed, capable base stealer.\n  Going to have 40 steals before we reach July. Might be a big time weapon on the bases.\n  Really, really like the bat. It's going to be a good major league caliber bat.\n  Will take walks and limit K's.\n  Defense is a very real concern, but should be able to handle the outfield fine and could fill in at 2B in a pinch. Could also see a move to 1B eventually.\n  Overall, I think this is a guy who could be a really solid number 2 type hitter in a lineup, but could find trouble trying to find a defensive home.",
    "Notes Updated 3": "44760",
    "Scouting Notes 3": "Really good bat to ball skills\n  Makes great swing decisions\n  Has pretty decent pop in the bat, but the swing is most likely not going to put up huge home run numbers. Line drive approach.\n  Not a good infield defender, would not feel very good about him at second base.\n  Surprisingly has looked solid in center field. Likely moves to left as he goes higher up the ranks.\n  Good speed, capable base stealer.",
